# Git Workflow

`{{DEFAULT_BRANCH}}` is protected. All work happens on a branch and lands through a PR. Remote: `{{OWNER_REPO}}`. Use `gh` for PR operations.

## Branching

Branch off freshly-pulled `{{DEFAULT_BRANCH}}`:

```txt
<type>/{{TICKET_REF_PATTERN}}-<short-kebab-slug>
```

- **type**: `feature`, `fix`, `chore`, `docs`, `refactor`
- **{{TICKET_REF_PATTERN}}**: the ticket reference<!-- e.g. "ABC-123" for Linear/Jira, "issue-12" for GitHub -->; omit when no ticket exists (`chore/update-readme`)

## Parallel tickets: worktrees

Running more than one ticket at a time? One worktree per ticket, one session per worktree; sessions never collide on a working tree:

```bash
git worktree add ../{{REPO_NAME}}-<ticket-ref> -b <branch> {{DEFAULT_BRANCH}}
# work there; after the PR merges:
git worktree remove ../{{REPO_NAME}}-<ticket-ref>
```

## Commits

- Imperative subject, capitalized, no trailing period, ≤ 72 chars: "Add invoice export", not "added".
- Body explains **why**, not a restatement of the diff.
- Ticket trailer: `{{COMMIT_TRAILER_EXAMPLE}}`<!-- e.g. "Refs ABC-123", or "Closes #12" when it completes the ticket -->.
- One logical change per commit.

## Before staging

`git diff --stat` first: if the diff is much larger than your change (format-on-save churn), revert the incidental noise and re-apply only the real change.

## Pushing & PRs

- Never push to `{{DEFAULT_BRANCH}}`; force-push only your own branch with `--force-with-lease`.
- Sync with `{{DEFAULT_BRANCH}}` before opening/updating a PR.
- Open PRs with `/create-pr` (a hook redirects raw `gh pr create`); description per the PR template.

